From abe20b1815d453b5148c78b616ea65accc4c074f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 08:38:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): [daveey] refuse model pins the managed routing
 registry rejects at create, not at worker startup

Under model_routing.enforce_subscription_only, kanban_create accepted a pin
(claude-sonnet-4-5) that pin_policy refuses; each worker then exited 1 at
startup and was retried as a transient crash until triage.

- validate_model_assignment runs pin_policy against the assignee's config, so
  create (tool, CLI, REST) and set-model refuse with code
  model_pin_not_in_routing_registry and list the allowed names.
- dispatch_guard reuses it: a bad pin already in the DB gets an assignment
  block before spawn (guard-hold exempt, like model_provider_mismatch).
- pin_policy raises ManagedPinRejectedError; a worker hitting it exits
  EX_CONFIG (terminal) instead of 1.
- kanban_create model description: leave it out unless another tier is
  needed; the name must be in the routing registry.
